extraction_notes: |
  - Experience ladder read off a render of printed 220 (cache p221), the column
    headed "NG Robot Control O.C.C.", lower bounds stored.
  - men_of_arms and occ_group: the book prints no O.C.C. grouping; its section
    heading on printed 76 is "Northern Gun O.C.C.s". Read as men of arms, as
    the book''s NG Police Officer and NG Loss Prevention Officer are: a
    corporate security force issued power armor that brings rogue robots down.
    The other reading, from the entry''s "part Operator and part Cowboy", is the
    Operator''s occ_group optional and men_of_arms false.
  - Special ability 2 (Psionics Amongst Robot Control Agents) is a pick-one
    group with percentile bands, with psionics_allowed false so the standard
    Random Psionics roll is not offered as well. The three Master Psychic bands
    grant their level-one powers by name and their level-two and level-three
    powers as schedule picks from exactly the named powers, then two powers a
    level from levels 4 to 15. The book prints I.S.P. (M.E. plus 2D6x10, +10
    per level) in the paragraph about the Master Psychic bands; it is stored on
    those three only. The Major and Minor bands print no I.S.P. and store none.
  - Psi-Ghost (level two, Robot Battler and Robot Whisperer) has no catalog
    row; it stays in each band''s description and is left out of the level-two
    schedule pick, which grants the other four.
  - Book names read as catalog rows: Telemechanic Mental Paralysis is
    Telemechanic Paralysis, Electro-Kinesis is Electrokinesis, Object Read is
    Object Read (Psychometry), Telekinesis Super is Telekinesis (Super),
    Bio-Manipulation is Bio-Manipulation (the evil eye).
  - O.C.C. Bonuses: +1 M.E. is stored; the +1 on Perception Rolls is limited to
    robot situations and is a special ability. Gut Instincts'' +2% to
    Electrical, Mechanical and Demolitions skills is prose, as is the +20% of
    Disable Robot Operating Systems, which applies only against robots.
  - Language: Native Language, American (+10%) is stored at the catalog''s 98%.
  - Pilot: one non-military vehicle of choice is a Pilot pick at +10%; the
    non-military limit is in the note and not enforced.
  - O.C.C. Related: Cowboy, Espionage, Horsemanship and Wilderness are None,
    so not listed.
  - Stored equipment: 1D6 E-Clips (the book gives 1D6 for each W.P. weapon;
    the W.P. of choice need not take E-Clips, so one roll is stored), laser
    torch, portable tool kit, walkie-talkie, compass and canteen. The weapons
    of choice, power pack, NG-S2 survival kit, I.D., body armor, nightvision
    goggles, bugs, camera, field computer, boots, power armor and hovercycle or
    robot horse are a choice or have no catalog row; they are in the body.
  - starting_money is one month''s pay, 5,000 credits, as printed.
  - Skill bases are catalog base plus the printed bonus, already added.
---

## Lore

Robot Control agents are Northern Gun''s robot wranglers, part Operator and part Cowboy. When a drone, a sabotaged combat robot, or a drunk merc in power armor runs amok, Robot Control brings it down fast while keeping collateral damage low. An agent may talk a robot pilot down or distract him while a partner sneaks around to cut the vehicle''s power or knock out its sensors and targeting, or may lure a runaway machine away from people and property until heavier forces arrive.

Alignment: Any, but the vast majority are Principled, Scrupulous or Unprincipled. A high P.E. and Spd can come in handy but are not required. Most official agents are human, though 20% are D-Bees of varying types.

## Equipment

A Northern Gun weapon of choice for each W.P. with 1D6 extra E-Clips for each, laser torch, portable tool kit, one NG Power Pack (any type), NG-S2 survival kit, I.D. and credentials, light or medium NG body armor of choice, walkie-talkie, nightvision goggles, 2 auditory listening bugs, 1 micro-video camera, field computer, compass, canteen, hiking boots and personal items.

Standard issue also includes one suit of Samson or other light or medium NG power armor of choice, and a hovercycle (any NG brand) or a robot horse (any NG or Bandito Arms knock-off brand); many agents ride their robot horses without any cosmetic hide. Agents have limited access to other Northern Gun products, including explosives and heavy weapons, on special assignment, seldom heavy combat robots or prototypes.

## Pay and cybernetics

Pay is 5,000 NGMI credits a month plus bonuses for outstanding field work, and NG usually pays medical bills for injuries on the job. Characters start with one month''s pay.

Unless the agent is a psychic who fears implants will impair his powers, many have cybernetic or minor bionic implants, and the company pays for bionic or Bio-System replacements for parts lost in the line of duty. All bionic augmentation must be authorized by the company, though as many as eight legal cybernetic enhancements are allowed. Only 5% are partial cyborgs and there are no Combat Cyborgs on the force; Headhunters, Juicers, Crazies, Psi-Techs and other augmented warriors are hired as independent contractors.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ng-robot-control');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ng-robot-control';

